 > Error `statusText` should be short (max 512 to 1024 characters) and only include tab, spaces or visible ASCII characters and extended characters (byte value 128–255). Prefer `message` in JSON body for extended message.
 
+### Problem Details
+
+With `new H3({ problemDetails: true })`, errors are sent as `application/problem+json` ([RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457)):
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "https://example.com/probs/forbidden",
+  "title": "Forbidden",
+  "status": 403,
+  "detail": "Not authenticated",
+  "instance": "/accounts/42"
+}
+```
+
+`message` is sent as `detail` (omitted when it only repeats the status text), `statusText` as `title`, and `data` and `body` keys as extension members that cannot override the standard ones. Unhandled errors only include `type`, `title`, `status` and `instance`.
+
 ## Unhandled Errors
 
 Any error that occurs during calling [request lifecycle](/guide/basics/lifecycle) without using `HTTPError` will be processed as an _unhandled_ error.
